s given by the same formula independent of the choice\nof the topology <MATH_0004>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nProof of (1). Let <MATH_0005>,\n<MATH_0006> be a diagram. Write\n<MATH_0007> so we get a diagram\n<MATH_0008>.\nThen <MATH_0009> in\n<MATH_0010> for\n<MATH_0011>\nby Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThis proves (1).\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nProof of (2). Write <MATH_0012> and\n<MATH_0013> with <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015>\nquasi-coherent on <MATH_0016>. Then\n<MATH_0017> in\n<MATH_0018> for\n<MATH_0019>\nby Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThis proves (2).\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nProof of (3). Let <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021> be in\n<MATH_0022>. Write\n<MATH_0023> with <MATH_0024>\nquasi-coherent on <MATH_0025>. By\nLemma <REF_0005> we have\n<MATHSEG_0001> finite locally free in fppf topology<MATHSEG_0002> finite locally free on <MATHSEG_0003> finite locally free in <MATHSEG_0004>tale topology<MATHSEG_0005> finite locally free on <MATHSEG_0006> finite locally free in Zariski topology<MATHSEG_0007>\nThis explains the parenthetical statement of part (3).\nNow, if these equivalent conditions hold, then <MATH_0026>\nis finite locally free. The construction of\n<MATH_0027> in\nModules on Sites, Section <REF_0006>\ndepends only on <MATH_0028> and <MATH_0029> as presheaves\nof modules (only whether the output <MATH_0030> is\na sheaf depends on whether <MATH_0031> and <MATH_0032> are\nsheaves).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:af9c998b98015dede2d834021dec14043f0a26bbdc96c909c81b01bf7ccb356f", "unit_id": "tag:0GNE:proof"}
